\subsection{Usage Grids and Target Placement}
\label{app:interleaved_details}

The Tiger, Diagnosis and Bandit calibration curves use zero plus $15$ logarithmically spaced positive weights from $10^{-3}$ to $100$, for $16$ grid points. Their planning horizons are $6$, $3$ and $2$, respectively. The shadow-price and held-out frontier studies share this grid and these horizons (\texttt{make\_\allowbreak log\_\allowbreak w\_\allowbreak grid} in \texttt{rho\_\allowbreak aif/\allowbreak budget.py}, \texttt{experiments/\allowbreak run\_\allowbreak budget\_\allowbreak frontier.py}).
